  "notes": "Schema source: official iSafetyBench data repository (github.com/iSafetyBench/data) - annotations_hazard.json / annotations_normal.json records are {video_name, caption, gt_actions[]}; actions.txt defines 98 routine actions in 8 groups and 67 hazard actions in 10 groups (counts match design_v3 F-26). MAPPING IS A DRAFT pending developer approval (design_v3 C0 review stop) and pending validation against the actual downloaded snapshot (schema read from the official repository, not from a local download; the loader validates keys loudly and aborts on any deviation). Justifications: pedestrian_vehicle <- vehicle events where a person is struck/dragged/crushed or a collision/near-miss occurs (person-on-foot vs vehicle core). no_ppe <- EMPTY: the 67-action hazard taxonomy contains no PPE-violation action (only routine 'putting on/taking off PPE'); no_ppe rows will carry no positives from this dataset - flagged here explicitly for the developer. blocked_exit <- 'cluttered workspace' (obstruction of walking/driving space by stored objects; nearest available proxy for blocked aisles/exits). unsafe_load <- the six load-integrity actions (falling/slipping/breaking loads, toppling shelves, suspended-load crane imbalance, truck-load fall). fall_or_spill <- person falls/slips ('person falling down', 'hanging from something after slip', 'carrying object and slipping') plus 'flooded floor' as the only liquid/floor hazard. SUBSET-RULE NOTE (strict design reading): a hazard-file clip tagged with ANY unmapped hazard action is excluded entirely even when it also carries a mapped action; the loader additionally reports the count of such would-be-kept clips so the developer can revisit this rule at mapping review. 15 of 67 hazard actions are mapped; 52 listed as unmapped; all 98 routine actions are clean-negative candidates."
